WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.600
She's gained acclaim for films from The Wolf
of Wall Street to Once Upon a Time in Hollywood,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.280
but how much do you really know about this
multi-talented leading lady?

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.080
From her humble origins to her latest releases,
this is the true story of Margot Robbie.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.600
The fact that Margot Robbie is Australian
can come as a surprise to even the most ardent

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.100
fan.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.840
Of course, it's probably a testament to her
skill as an actor that this central part of

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.720
her life is so well-camouflaged.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.499
People often think of Robbie with Tonya Harding's
flat intonation, or Harley Quinn's charmingly

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.620
nasal sing-song voice.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.320
What they don't realize is that she's as positively
Aussie as they come.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.250
Robbie grew up in the Gold Coast hinterland,
part of the state of Queensland and known

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.260
worldwide for its natural beauty.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.360
Everything from rainforest hikes, wine tasting
experiences, and bird-watching trips are enjoyed

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.810
by the countless number of tourists who flock
to this part of Australia every year but Robbie

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.040
herself spent much of her childhood working.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.460
One of four children raised by a single mother,
Robbie grew up traveling between her mother's

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.320
house and her grandparents' farm.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.079
Since her mother's family raised grain and
her father's family farmed sugarcane and mangoes,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.680
she grew up tending to a wide variety of crops.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.560
Funnily enough, this actually ended up helping
her during filming on the post-apocalyptic

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.340
drama Z for Zachariah.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.580
As she joked in an interview with Vanity Fair:

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.460
"I already knew how to drive a tractor and
milk cows."

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.720
To most of the world, it would seem like Robbie
has had a meteoric rise in Hollywood from

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:29.200
The Wolf of Wall Street to Once Upon a Time
in Hollywood, she's dominated the cineplex

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.240
for the past few years with a treasure trove
of distinctive roles.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.380
Crass figure skating legend?

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.120
Done.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.060
Queen Elizabeth the First at the height of
her rivalry with Mary, Queen of Scots?

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:39.560
Check.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.800
Sharon Tate at the apex of her career?

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.640
Bringo.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.580
And given her 2020-and-beyond slate is filled
up with roles like the eponymous doll in Barbie,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.560
she doesn't show any sign of slowing down
soon, either.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:54.720
But in her native Australia, it took all that
buzz just to get people to stop thinking of

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.980
her as a soap opera star.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.000
Cast in 2008 as Donna Freedman on Neighbours,
Robbie saw the character through from guest

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:02.390
part to recurring role.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.740
A confident, slightly goofy character, Robbie
turned Donna into a fan favorite who audiences

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.600
loved to watch mature from teen fangirl into
fiery young woman.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.519
She did it so well, in fact, that she garnered
a Logie Award for Popular Actress and acclaim

00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:20.280
for portraying Freedman's bisexuality with
compassion and courage.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.770
To most of the world, Robbie is a bona fide
movie star but to many Australians, she'll

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.780
always be Donna.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.720
The routes to stardom are many and varied.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.860
Sometimes all an actor really needs is one
chance to show their stuff.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.100
Sometimes they're the right person's friend.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.160
Sometimes they have a unique skill that no
one else can offer.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.640
And sometimes, they're just enormously, heart-warmingly
earnest.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.540
Robbie has walked more than one path on her
way to stardom, but that last tack taken might

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.880
be the most important of all.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:48.940
As she told Vogue:

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.780
"I've always been a huge huge Tarantino fan."

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.260
So huge, in fact, that Robbie vowed to send
him a letter expressing her appreciation once

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.640
she thought she'd gained enough prominence
to do so.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.340
After producing and starring in the award-winning
I, Tonya, Robbie felt she had the backing

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.180
to reach out to the legendary director.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.300
She later recalled:

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.599
“So I wrote him and said, ‘I adore your
films, and I would love to work with you in

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.540
some capacity.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:13.700
Or any capacity.”

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.820
"Ohhhhhh, That's a bingo!"

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:23.560
Tarantino was charmed, Robbie was game, and
the exchange led to her taking the role of

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.940
Sharon Tate in Once Upon a Time in Hollywood.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.460
Just goes to show that, sometimes, all it
takes is an honest word.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.439
One thing Margot Robbie's life story has made
very clear is her drive and commitment to

00:03:35.439 --> 00:03:37.040
everything she puts her name to.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.860
It pushes her into increasingly demanding
acting roles, fascinating character choices,

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.560
and even some surprising hobbies.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.700
But her energy isn't confined to her work
in front of the camera Robbie has also thrown

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.180
herself wholeheartedly into movie production
as well.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.080
Founded in 2017, her LuckyChap Entertainment
production company hit the ground running

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.359
in a major way.

00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:02.260
Though Birds of Prey will be their most high-profile
early release, LuckyChap has already sold

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.260
its half-hour series Dollface, starring Kat
Dennings, to Hulu.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:10.560
They've also premiered the company's indie
thriller Dreamland, and are gearing up for

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.940
Barbie, starring Robbie as the titular doll.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.820
Being involved on the production side of Hollywood
is the dream for many actors, but the passion,

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.580
dedication, and sheer tenacity it demands
tends to deter most of them.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:22.800
Not Robbie, though.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.620
LuckyChap is involved in an ever-expanding
slate of projects over the next few years,

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.660
nearly all of them centering around women.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:33.919
And since Robbie has been wowing audiences
for years with her performing acumen, the

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.300
chances are good she'll flourish behind the
camera, too.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.220
Suicide Squad's lackluster reviews didn't
matter much when it came to Harley Quinn's

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:41.800
own fate.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.240
Even years after its release, Halloween is
still pretty much just a gathering of Daddy's

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.080
Little Monsters all sporting Robbie's signature
two-tone pigtails.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:55.360
On top of that, Quinn is set to claim an animated
series all her own, and Robbie will star in

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.860
Birds of Prey without the Joker in tow.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.020
Robbie isn't just starring in and producing
Birds of Prey, however she developed and pitched

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.509
it herself to DC after Suicide Squad's debut.

00:05:06.509 --> 00:05:07.000
In 2018, she remarked:

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.500
"I pitched the idea of an R-rated girl gang
film including Harley, because I was like,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:12.480
'Harley needs friends.'

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:16.600
Harley loves interacting with people, so don't
ever make her do a standalone film.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.120
She's got to be with other people, it should
be a girl gang."

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:23.900
As snippets of the inventive costume design
and hugely exciting casting leaked into a

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.669
Harley-hungry internet, the movie's anticipation
only has only proved Robbie right: The world

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:32.140
wants superheroines, and she's the woman to
deliver it to them.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:38.060
Suicide Squad's production and subsequent
promotion was as much of an event as the movie

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:38.560
itself.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.460
Jared Leto shocked his castmates by offering
them disturbing, in-character gifts.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.470
Posters featured everything from psychedelic
cereal bowls to mushroom clouds.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:52.550
Perhaps most dramatic of all, however, were
the tattoos many of the cast got matching

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:59.879
"SKWAD" tattoos - spelled S-K-W-A-D because…
well, misspellings are cool? - to commemorate

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.940
their time together.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:05.740
This sparked a new interest for Robbie, and
now the star has given tattoos to a number

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:10.080
of friends, colleagues, and loved ones using
a tattoo gun she bought on eBay.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.879
"Well, at first I really had to beg people
and then it became a thing and people approach

00:06:16.879 --> 00:06:19.210
me now and say yeah, I’ll get one it’ll
be funny."

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:23.289
Though she doesn't claim much in the way of
skill and actually alleges that she might

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:26.640
be "getting worse", her interest in the art
of ink is real.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:32.080
If you're willing to get into Robbie's chair,
like buddy Cara Delevingne was, you might

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.970
just find yourself with something as innocuous
as smiley faces on the bottom of your toes.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:40.520
Of course, according to Robbie, they tend
to rub off in a few days due to the nature

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.780
of the soles of the feet, so hey why not do
what Harley would do and take a wild chance?

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.700
Actors garner a lot of odd skills over the
course of their careers.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:53.740
And Robbie is no exception: Suicide Squad
had her doing "a tremendous amount of her

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.120
own stunts," according to producer Richard
Suckle.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:56.940
He explained:

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.080
"I went on set and I was watching the monitor
and the camera was moving but she was doing

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.360
something that I could've sworn, for sure,
she had to be in a harness, and, I kid you

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.020
not, she was not in a harness."

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:11.720
The sequence Suckle is referring to here is
the infamous elevator scene in which Harley

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:15.300
runs up the side of an elevator wall and backflips
onto a bad guy.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.720
That's right: That was Robbie herself, defying
gravity in spiked heels and a face full of

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:21.220
makeup.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:26.120
But that's not even the most impressive feat
she pulled off as part of DC's zany ode to

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.860
the scum of the superheroic world.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:34.240
In order to film a pivotal underwater scene,
Robbie worked with a free diver and learned

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.490
to hold her breath for an extended period
of time.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:40.280
"But I could do a resting breath hold of 5
minutes which meant I could do a…

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.069
“You could hold your breath for 5 minutes?”

00:07:42.069 --> 00:07:42.560
“Yeah!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.820
Which I never thought was possible."

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.700
Robbie might play a clown, but she certainly
doesn't train like one.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:53.639
Robbie's character in The Wolf of Wall Street,
Naomi LaPaglia, is basically a life-size Barbie,

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:58.060
both in her beautiful blonde looks and in
the way her husband, Leonardo DiCaprio's Jordan

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.980
Belfort, treats her like more of a possession
than a person.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.760
And Robbie ended up connecting to the character
best through, of all things, manicures.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:11.199
After her acting coach told her to imagine
having just had her nails done, Robbie found

00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:16.020
herself immediately able to channel the character's
brash Brooklyn attitude, and she ultimately

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:18.700
requested acrylic nails to further her performance.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.140
She told The New York Times:

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:23.750
"You can't tuck your hair back the way you
would, you can't wipe away tears the way you

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.090
would, because you've got nails that are an
inch long."

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:29.900
That's not the only quirk that helped along
her performance, though: She also indulged

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:33.080
in a little liquid courage for some of her
more revealing scenes.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.120
She later remarked:

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.260
"I did three shots of tequila and then took
my clothes off and did the scene and I was

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:38.760
fine.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.060
Acting 101: three shots of tequila and you'll
be fine."

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:47.620
In the age of the omnipresent superhero, more
than one actor has pulled double (or even

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:48.240
triple) duty.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:53.880
Chris Evans, Marvel's beloved Captain America,
played the Human Torch in 2005's Fantastic

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:54.380
Four.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:59.360
Samuel L. Jackson played the sort of psychotic
monster Nick Fury usually works to thwart

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.860
as the Octopus in 2008's The Spirit.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:06.320
Ben Affleck might not be Batman anymore, but
he'll probably always be the only guy who

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.320
can say he played both the Dark Knight and
Daredevil.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.800
Margot Robbie never actually got that far,
but she came close when she passed on playing

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.580
Sue Storm in 2015's Fantastic Four.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.050
She told the New York Daily News:

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.840
"I didn't really resonate with the script.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.320
But I had a great meeting with the director
and I really enjoyed that.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.800
I guess it's part of the game: Sometimes you
win some, sometimes you lose some."

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.460
And you can't help but wonder if she might
feel as though she dodged a bullet.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:35.240
Fantastic Four, in which Kate Mara played
Sue Storm, ended up a critical disaster and

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.720
a box office bomb, with no further installments
in sight.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.660
Margot Robbie is no stranger to the physical
demands of the actor's life.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.740
She learned to ice skate like an Olympian
for the title role in I, Tonya, in addition

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.220
to taking part in rigorous weight training.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:53.320
Harley Quinn had her strapping on ankle weights
and exploring pilates.

00:09:53.339 --> 00:09:57.730
But there's one line she won't cross, and
she found it while preparing for her role

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.040
in The Legend of Tarzan.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.280
Producers wanted her Jane Porter, Tarzan's
legendary love interest, to look even more

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.610
slender than Robbie normally does.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:07.940
Robbie pushed back, arguing:

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:12.760
"It's the 19th century [in the film] if she's
got a bit of weight on her, it's probably

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.380
a good thing.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.040
I'm not going to look thin just for the sake
of it."

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:20.640
Robbie got her way, and her Jane Porter is
a ferocious delight to behold.

